\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20.1.1}{\ignorespaces Zoom on \(t_9\) right after \(\text  {range-add }[2..5]\mathrel {+}=3\). \(t_9\)'s aggregate is already \(15\) (folded), its \(+3\) sits \emph  {only} in its tag, so its two leaves \(t_{18},t_{19}\) still show the OLD values \(4,5\) -- \textbf  {stale by \(+3\)}, shown by the dashed orange edge. \texttt  {rquery} that covers \(t_9\) whole never touches those leaves (it returns \(15\)); \texttt  {rquery} that overlaps \(t_9\) \emph  {partially} must \texttt  {push}, turning \(t_{18},t_{19}\) into \(7,8\) and clearing the tag. \(t_{17}\) (leaf \(A_2\)) was written directly to \(5\) because the update reached it on the partial end -- no tag sits above it.}}{1221}{figure.caption.216}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c15-push}{{20.1.1}{1221}{Zoom on \(t_9\) right after \(\text {range-add }[2..5]\mathrel {+}=3\). \(t_9\)'s aggregate is already \(15\) (folded), its \(+3\) sits \emph {only} in its tag, so its two leaves \(t_{18},t_{19}\) still show the OLD values \(4,5\) -- \textbf {stale by \(+3\)}, shown by the dashed orange edge. \code {rquery} that covers \(t_9\) whole never touches those leaves (it returns \(15\)); \code {rquery} that overlaps \(t_9\) \emph {partially} must \code {push}, turning \(t_{18},t_{19}\) into \(7,8\) and clearing the tag. \(t_{17}\) (leaf \(A_2\)) was written directly to \(5\) because the update reached it on the partial end -- no tag sits above it}{figure.caption.216}{}}
