\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20.4.1}{\ignorespaces The shared tree \(T\) (opener, Ch.~12--17). Preorder gives \(\tin  =(1,2,6,3,4,7,8,5,9,10)\), so \(\subtree  (2)=\{2,4,5,8\}\) is exactly the \emph  {contiguous} Euler slice \(E[2..5]=(2,4,5,8)\) -- the orange bracket. Painting \(2\)'s subtree is one lazy range update on those four cells; no recursion into the tree, only Ch.~5's precomputed \(\tin  /\tout  \) and \(Code~\ref {lst:c15-assign}\)'s paint.}}{1247}{figure.caption.220}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c15-subtree}{{20.4.1}{1247}{The shared tree \(T\) (opener, Ch.~12--17). Preorder gives \(\tin =(1,2,6,3,4,7,8,5,9,10)\), so \(\subtree (2)=\{2,4,5,8\}\) is exactly the \emph {contiguous} Euler slice \(E[2..5]=(2,4,5,8)\) -- the orange bracket. Painting \(2\)'s subtree is one lazy range update on those four cells; no recursion into the tree, only Ch.~5's precomputed \(\tin /\tout \) and \(\coderef {c15-assign}\)'s paint}{figure.caption.220}{}}
